{"actual_contract_can_pass_while_concern_fails":"NO_WITHIN_CITED_OPERATIVE_CONTRACT","candidate_id":"T8C-CHEAP","canonical_adjudication_and_final_review_pending":true,"concern":"Smallest adequate architecture and coordination machinery","decision_authority":"NONE_PREPARATION_FOR_CANONICAL_CURRENT_SUBJECT_REVIEW","historical_prepared_contract_anchors":[{"line_end":71,"line_start":41,"rockstar":"R0029","scope":"Exact excerpt; use with complete current body and ordered normative comments","text":"> Spend scarce reasoning where it materially changes engineering judgement; compile sufficient source context, authority, decision rationale, acceptance, verification, rollback and STOP conditions into a durable executable artifact; when several valid executor routes exist, choose the least-cost sufficiently capable route; escalate when delegated capability proves insufficient; and measure whether the split reduced cost, context or rediscovery without degrading correctness, evidence, authority or recoverability.

Correctness and evidence remain primary. Cost cannot authorize a weaker result.

## Trigger and cheap path

Trigger only when:

- more than one valid executor/model/route is actually available;
- the work separates judgement-heavy planning from bounded mechanical execution;
- capability or context mismatch is a material failure risk;
- the artifact is expected to be reused across interruption, handoff, worktree or agent boundaries; or
- execution cost/context/latency is material enough that a different valid route could change the engineering decision.

Non-trigger / cheap path:

- only one valid executor is available;
- task is small, reversible and direct;
- executor choice cannot materially change cost, correctness or reconstructibility;
- gathering capability/cost data would cost more than the plausible saving;
- no delegation occurs.

No mandatory worksheet or model comparison is created on the cheap path.

## Authority and evidence boundary

- Model or executor availability does not grant mutation authority.
- Capability labels, price tables, provider marketing and nominal model tiers are leads, not proof of task fitness.
- The plan/work order carries authority boundaries; it does not create new authority.
- Executor self-report cannot prove sufficient capability or completion.
- Reviewer verifies live source, diff, tests and acceptance evidence.","url":"https://github.com/theislampill/IMPLEMENTAUDIT.md/issues/190"},{"line_end":307,"line_start":307,"rockstar":"R0022","scope":"Exact excerpt; use with complete current body and ordered normative comments","text":"R0022 is done only when every acceptance row has evidence on the exact merged source and installed/package surface it affects; warranted-control, cheap-path, artefact-consumer, review-yield, evidence-reuse, parallelism, retirement, expected-risk, anti-volume, and anti-worksheet controls pass; external-validity results and limits are recorded; and exact-tree independent review passes.","url":"https://github.com/theislampill/IMPLEMENTAUDIT.md/issues/163"}],"material_binding_required":"Retain qualified checker slice under exact-byte guard. Do not create a ceremony layer to qualify cheapness; one representative triggered/non-triggered host discriminator is sufficient when shared coverage is justified.","new_durable_identity_proposed":false,"primary_source_properties":[{"key":"EAOSE:EAOSE-C017","pointer":"EVOLVED_AMA_INTER_CROSSWALK_INTAKE.json#/rows/162","row_sha256":"b28ef6690fbb2bbb1134189bc159084bbb1a2afc1718d1aafba0de65d40e582a"},{"key":"EAOSE:EAOSE-C068","pointer":"EVOLVED_AMA_INTER_CROSSWALK_INTAKE.json#/rows/213","row_sha256":"13da6ec9110d4eede403c98c9931d44b40eaf24d38362fcffc5a600b23c66d20"},{"key":"EMAS:EMAS-001","pointer":"EVOLVED_AMA_INTER_CROSSWALK_INTAKE.json#/rows/70","row_sha256":"7ac0a9700d177e9135c378f28348bb676a868f27549a61c11041b280fe4f55de"},{"key":"EMAS:EMAS-019","pointer":"EVOLVED_AMA_INTER_CROSSWALK_INTAKE.json#/rows/88","row_sha256":"41e3fe0dda2919bfa099dd4f130223baf8a0ad98ab094fb88f1ef12b2339b812"},{"key":"EMAS:EMAS-065","pointer":"EVOLVED_AMA_INTER_CROSSWALK_INTAKE.json#/rows/134","row_sha256":"200a0292817a1e130c804e0446180c20a1cc4b4369ffb88ba63a29f345310c19"},{"key":"EWM:EWM-004","pointer":"EVOLVED_BWP_INTER_CROSSWALK_INTAKE.json#/rows/76","row_sha256":"c19eb7f